t rollouts; distillation methods query a frozen teacher at the same student prefixes. Evaluation benchmarks and metrics. We evaluate AIME24–26, MATH500 ( Lightman et al., 2024 ) and OlympiadBench(math,english) ( He et al., 2024 ) for mathematical reasoning and GPQA-Diamond ( Rein et al., 2023 ) and MBPP+ ( Liu et al., 2023 ) for out-of-distribution transfer. Avg@32 is the mean accuracy over 32 responses per problem and Pass@32 the fraction of problems solved by at least one; OOD columns report Avg@32 in Table 1 and Pass@32 in Table 3 . Additional mathematical benchmarks are reported with Avg@8 or Pass@8 as indicated. Variance and statistical-significance analyses for the AIME evaluations are provided in Appendix J . We compare with GRPO ( Shao et al., 2024 ) , OPD ( Agarwal et al., 2024a ) , OPSD ( Zhao et al., 2026b ) , EOPD ( Jin et al., 2026 ) , and KD ( Hinton et al., 2015 ; Kim and Rush, 2016 ) , as applicable. The 4B non-thinking setting also reports pure RKL and FKL objectives. Within each comparison, methods share initialization, prompts, rollout budget, decoding, and evaluation protocol, and teacher-based methods share the same teacher. 6.2 Non-thinking student results Table 1: Results for non-thinking students (accuracy %). Shaded rows denote OC-OPD. Dashes indicate scores not present in the supplied results. Δ \Delta reports the Qwen3-4B gain over EOPD in percentage points, computed from the displayed scores. Methods Math (I.D.) O.O.D. AIME 2024 AIME 2025 AIME 2026 MATH500 OlympiadBench GPQA D MBPP + + Avg@32 Pass@32 Avg@32 Pass@32 Avg@32 Pass@32 Avg@8 Pass@8 Avg@32 Teacher: Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507 Qwen3-1.7B 14.16 43.33 9.90 30.00 7.71 23.33 71.88 52.67 29.59 56.03 + GRPO 34.17 70.00 25.52 46.67 26.04 50.00 82.21 62.57 — — + OPD 31.98 73.33 20.73 50.00 23.54 46.67 85.84 60.77 — — + OPSD 33.33 73.33 22.60 53.33 21.35 56.67 86.20 64.84 — — + OC-OPD 41.67 76.67 34.38 63.33 30.31 76.67 87.40 67.40 34.01 59.01 Qwen3-4B 23.85 56.67 22.40 56.67 15.10 53.33 